{
, "summary": "The text covers the Group's credit risk management policy, including accurate risk ratings, financial analytics, and product mix management to avoid concentration. It details the Expected Credit Loss (ECL) model under Ind AS 109, applicable to amortized cost and fair value debt assets, excluding ULIP portfolios. It explains the 12-month ECL approach, 75% Loss Given Default assumption, recognition in profit and loss, absence of POCI assets, and simplified approach for other items. It provides ECL allowance movement figures. It discusses liquidity risk, asset-liability mismatch, cash flow sources, governance via ALM Committee, and ALM techniques. It presents maturity profiles for financial liabilities and insurance contract liabilities, and mentions market risk including equity and interest rate risks."
}
